 __“Her seed”__ stands alone in the Torah, for Scripture reckons seed by the father; no genealogy runs through a mother.
 Read the letters again and the anomaly resolves: the seed of the _ishah_ is the seed of the _esh_ — the fire.
-And when the promise was kept, both readings met in one womb: the virgin supplied the flesh, and the seed no man fathered was conceived __“of the *Holy Ghost*”__ (Matthew 1:20) — __“the power of the Highest shall *overshadow* thee”__ (Luke 1:35) — the God who is __“a *consuming fire*”__ (Hebrews 12:29) giving the woman the seed she could not have.
